  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the inverse of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{4}x-1?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{4}x-1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}y-1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{4}y-1 \\\\ x+1 & =\\frac{1}{4}y \\\\ 4(x+1) & =y \\\\ 4x+4 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=4x+4\n$$",
